<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The target board (uitarget.py): the name of the character or monster
	     the player clicked, a monster's HP and, for another player, its
	     portrait, class and guild (the modern looks) and the relation
	     buttons (whisper, exchange, fight, friend, party, guild).
	     While the target flag is on, the game window makes the facade
	     nui_target.TargetBoard (controller assets/root/nui_target.py). The
	     exchange button shows while the target is within the exchange range,
	     which C++ watches (the in_range key follows the target.in_range
	     feed), where legacy measured it every frame. Nothing takes the
	     focus, so the buttons act on mousedown; Escape closes the board in
	     its legacy place in the Escape chain (nui_hud.EscapeProxy). The
	     classic art is under d:/ymir work/ (assets/ETC).
	     Wave 10: the HP bar's orange damage trail drains by a transition
	     (NOVA-208; trail and trail_snap), its tint follows the feeds
	     target.poisoned and target.burning, the archer gauge below the
	     board the feed target.arrow_percent (NOVA-209), and a metin stone's
	     board shows the attack queue hint (NOVA-216). -->
	<title>target</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="target.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="nui-overlay nui-below-legacy-ui target" data-model="target">
	<div class="target__wrap">
		<div id="target-board" class="target-board nui-board nui-board--tooltip nui-fx nui-interactive" data-class-target-board--hp="show_hp" data-class-target-board--level="level > 0"
			data-class-target-board--buttons="size(buttons) > 0" data-class-target-board--player="portrait != ''" data-class-target-board--numbers="hp_values != ''"
			data-class-target-board--hint="hint != ''">
			<div class="target-board__head">
				<!-- The modern head: a monster's level in a badge, its name with
				     its grade, its HP in percent; the HP bar below the head.
				     Classic shows legacy's whole name (level and grade in front)
				     and the legacy gauge beside it instead. -->
				<span id="target-level" class="target-board__badge" data-if="level > 0"><span
					class="target-board__level">{{ level }}</span></span>
				<span id="target-name" class="target-board__name">{{ name }}</span>
				<span id="target-title" class="target-board__title">{{ title }}</span>
				<span id="target-element" data-if="element > 0" data-attr-class="'target-board__element target-board__element--' + element">{{ element_name }}</span>
				<button id="target-info" class="nui-button nui-button--ghost nui-button--icon nui-anim target-board__info" data-if="show_info"
					data-event-mousedown="info(ev.button)">?</button>
				<span id="target-values" class="target-board__values" data-if="hp_values != ''">{{ hp_values }}</span>
				<span id="target-percent" class="target-board__pct" data-if="show_hp">{{ hp * 100 | format(0) }}%</span>
				<!-- Classic's legacy gauge, tinted as the bar below, with the
				     damage trail over its empty part (the legacy orange art). -->
				<span class="target-board__hp-box" data-if="show_hp"><progress id="target-hp" class="nui-gauge nui-gauge--red target-board__hp"
					direction="right" data-attr-value="hp" data-class-is-poisoned="poisoned" data-class-is-burning="burning && !poisoned"/><span
					class="target-board__trail-track"><span id="target-trail-classic" class="target-board__trail nui-anim"
					data-attr-class="'target-board__trail nui-anim target-board__trail--' + trail + (trail_snap ? ' is-snap' : '')"
					data-style---target-hp="(hp * 100) + '%'"></span></span></span>
			</div>
			<!-- A player target's modern head, in place of the one above: the
			     portrait of its race in a round clip, its name over its class
			     and guild (no level: the client has none for another player).
			     Classic keeps the legacy head. -->
			<div id="target-player" class="target-board__player" data-if="portrait != ''">
				<span class="target-board__portrait"><img class="target-board__face" data-attr-src="portrait"/></span>
				<span class="target-board__meta"><span class="target-board__title">{{ title }}</span><span id="target-subtitle"
					class="target-board__sub" data-if="subtitle != ''">{{ subtitle }}</span></span>
				<span id="target-player-percent" class="target-board__pct" data-if="show_hp">{{ hp * 100 | format(0) }}%</span>
			</div>
			<button id="target-close" class="nui-button nui-button--ghost nui-button--icon nui-anim target-board__close"
				data-event-mousedown="close(ev.button)"><span class="nui-glyph nui-glyph--close target-board__glyph"><span
				class="nui-glyph__a"></span><span class="nui-glyph__b"></span></span></button>
			<!-- The HP bar: the gauge with its damage chip (green while the
			     target is poisoned, yellow while it burns), a sheen that crosses
			     the fill once every 4s, the empty part drawn over the sheen, the
			     orange damage trail from the HP to where it drains, and ticks at
			     every tenth. -->
			<div id="target-bar" class="target-board__bar" data-if="show_hp">
				<progress id="target-hp-bar" class="nui-gauge nui-gauge--red target-board__gauge" direction="right" data-attr-value="hp"
					data-class-is-poisoned="poisoned" data-class-is-burning="burning && !poisoned"/>
				<nui-blink class="target-board__sheen-clock" period="4"><span class="target-board__sheen nui-anim"></span></nui-blink>
				<progress class="target-board__cover" direction="left" data-attr-value="1 - hp"/>
				<span id="target-trail" class="target-board__trail nui-anim"
					data-attr-class="'target-board__trail nui-anim target-board__trail--' + trail + (trail_snap ? ' is-snap' : '')"
					data-style---target-hp="(hp * 100) + '%'"></span>
				<span class="target-board__ticks"></span>
			</div>
			<!-- A metin stone: Shift + right-click queues it (NOVA-216). -->
			<div id="target-hint" class="target-board__hint" data-if="hint != ''">{{ hint }}</div>
			<!-- The repeated slot reads only its index and top-level keys: RmlUi
			     updates a repeated element's own views with the data-for that
			     removes it, so when the list shrinks they could read an entry
			     that is gone. The button's views run after that removal. -->
			<div id="target-buttons" class="target-board__buttons" data-if="size(buttons) > 0">
				<div class="target-board__slot" data-for="b, i : buttons" data-if="i != exchange_at || in_range">
					<button class="nui-button nui-anim target-board__button" data-attr-id="'target-button-' + b.id"
						data-event-mousedown="press(b.id, ev.button)"><span class="target-board__label">{{ b.label }}</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>
			<!-- The archer gauge (NOVA-209) below the board while the player
			     holds a bow and has a target: empty at 80% arrow damage, full
			     at 120%, a mark at 100%; its tooltip says the bonus. -->
			<span id="target-arrow" class="target-arrow nui-has-tooltip nui-interactive" data-if="arrow_percent > 0"><progress
				id="target-arrow-gauge" class="target-arrow__gauge" direction="top" data-attr-value="(arrow_percent - 80) / 40"/><span
				class="target-arrow__mark"></span><span id="target-arrow-tip" class="nui-tooltip nui-anim target-arrow__tip"
				data-class-is-up="arrow_percent > 100" data-class-is-down="arrow_percent < 100">{{ arrow_pre }}{{ arrow_percent > 100 ? '+' : (100 > arrow_percent ? '-' : '') }}{{ arrow_percent > 100 ? arrow_percent - 100 : 100 - arrow_percent }}%{{ arrow_post }}</span></span>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
